HR Analytics – Employee Attrition Analysis

Project Overview

This project analyzes employee attrition using HR data to identify patterns and understand factors associated with employee turnover.

The objective is to help HR teams make data-driven decisions and improve employee retention.

Project Objectives

- Analyze overall employee attrition.
- Identify departments with high attrition rates.
- Analyze attrition across different job roles.
- Study the impact of overtime and job satisfaction.
- Explore employee demographics and work-related factors.
- Provide actionable business recommendations.

Dataset Information

- Dataset: IBM HR Employee Attrition Dataset
- Total Records: 1,470 employees
- Total Features: 35 columns
- Target Variable: Attrition

Tools & Technologies

- Python
- Google Colab
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn

Project Workflow

1. Data loading and exploration
2. Data cleaning and quality checks
3. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
4. Department-wise attrition analysis
5. Job-role-wise attrition analysis
6. Employee demographic analysis
7. Overtime and job satisfaction analysis
8. Data visualization
9. Business insights and recommendations

Key Findings

- Sales department recorded the highest attrition rate at 20.63%.
- Human Resources recorded 19.05% attrition.
- Research & Development recorded 13.84% attrition.
- Sales Representatives had the highest job-role attrition rate at 39.76%.

Business Recommendations

- Review sales targets, incentives, and employee workload.
- Improve retention strategies for high-attrition job roles.
- Monitor overtime and employee satisfaction.
- Provide career development and growth opportunities.
- Strengthen employee engagement initiatives.

Project Structure

- "HR_Analytics_Employee_Attrition.ipynb" – Python analysis notebook
